{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ci1SaWS5GgtRJLxrA1M41U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v5 â€” \"Durable Work\" â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\t> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / REVIEW / FIX / GATE history here. Seeded by\n4\t> Crucible at handoff 2026-06-14. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md` +\n5\t> `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (this folder).\n6\t\n7\t## Handoff (Crucible â†’ Foreman) â€” 2026-06-14\n8\t\n9\t- Builds on the merged v4.1 \"Project Cockpit\" + the terminal fixes (full-width fit,\n10\t  Ctrl+V paste, no-freeze pump).\n11\t- 6 waves, terminal wave = 6. test-command: `python -m pytest -v`.\n12\t- Grass design = the approved B+C hybrid (`_mockups/grass_catcher_refined.html`).\n13\t- **Verification is mandatory per UI wave:** rendered-DOM (positive+negative) +\n14\t  a real Playwright/Chromium interaction test + an orchestrator screenshot vs the\n15\t  mockup + user sign-off before merge. A string-grep gate is an automatic HALT.\n16\t  (Playwright is installed as a dev-only test dep; `pytest.importorskip`.)\n17\t\n18\t<!-- Foreman: append wave records below this line -->\n19\t\n20\t## Wave 1 â€” Run lifecycle: close-to-tile vs. deliberate hard-kill â€” GREEN (2026-06-14)\n21\t\n22\t- **EXECUTE** (fresh sub-agent): panel header rebuilt to THREE distinct controls\n23\t  (`â€“` minimize Â· `Ã—` CLOSE close-to-tile Â· `ðŸ—‘` KILL, confirm-gated â†’ term_kill).\n24\t  Re-added `#sessionBar` as the reopen vector for LIVE managed sessions (not\n25\t  server-rendered board tiles); `closePanel` (non-killing) vs `killPanel`\n26\t  (confirm + term_kill + `_removeSessionTile`); `renderSessionBar` rebuilds\n27\t  reopenable chips from MANAGED. New `tests/test_run_lifecycle.py` (DOM +\n28\t  Playwright + backend registry/PTY + token gate). Flipped the stale v4.1\n29\t  `sessionBar`-absent negative in `test_project_window.py` (FWM negatives intact).\n30\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 651 passed, 1 skipped (baseline 643+1, +8).\n31\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): 1 BLOCKER** â€” a hard-killed session\n32\t  is marked `done` (terminal) but its record is kept; `repopulate()` (term_sessions\n33\t  returns every status) re-synced it into the live bar ~400ms after kill, so the\n34\t  killed chip REAPPEARED. The Playwright test raced past it (closed the browser\n35\t  before `setTimeout(repopulate,400)` fired) â†’ GREEN on broken behavior (the v4\n36\t  timing-blind-gate trap). All other 6 scrutiny points CONFIRMED-OK (close never\n37\t  reaps; kill reaps no orphan; reopen re-attaches live PTY; stdlib-only; no\n38\t  Playwright in product; never :8777).\n39\t- **FIX (orchestrator):** `repopulate()` excludes terminal-status sessions\n40\t  (`_isTerminalStatus` mirrors `session_registry.TERMINAL_STATUSES` = {done,\n41\t  failed}) from the live bar; a session that just went terminal is evicted from\n42\t  MANAGED. Strengthened the Playwright kill assertion to wait 900ms (past the\n43\t  repopulate) and re-assert the chip + panel stay gone.\n44\t- **RE-GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 651 passed, 1 skipped. UI verified:\n45\t  rendered-DOM (positive `#sessionBar`/`#panelStack` + negative old `Ã— == kill`),\n46\t  real Playwright openâ†’closeâ†’reopenâ†’kill, and an orchestrator screenshot of the\n47\t  panel header showing the grey `Ã—` and a distinct red `ðŸ—‘` (visually confirmed).\n48\t- **COMMIT (scoped):** `dd08c6b` â€” anchor_gui.py + test_run_lifecycle.py +\n49\t  test_project_window.py only (no runtime churn).\n50\t\n51\t## Wave 2 â€” Past-session view: real summary + \"Continue in a live session\" â€” GREEN (2026-06-14)\n52\t\n53\t- **EXECUTE** (fresh sub-agent): (A) `summarizer.summarize_session` extended with\n54\t  three DETERMINISTIC source-grounded fields â€” `skill` / `prompts` / `actions`\n55\t  (read straight off session+member records, NEVER through the model â†’ zero\n56\t  fabrication; honest empty/placeholder when absent). Model `claims` still go\n57\t  through generate-twice + grounding filter; failed-runner branch still skips the\n58\t  cache (no poison). (B) Historical panel JS (`_mountReadOnlyBody` rewritten â†’\n59\t  `_renderPastSession`/`_fillPastSessionDetail`) replaces the \"session complete\"\n60\t  dead-end with skill+prompts+files+doc-role links. (C) New token-gated\n61\t  `POST /api/rnd/continue_session` (+ `_build_continue_seed`) â†’ `start_session` in\n62\t  the SAME lane seeded with the prior summary; original never mutated (R2).\n63\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 660 passed, 1 skipped (baseline 651+1, +9).\n64\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): SHIP â€” 0 BLOCKER, 2 MINOR.** All 7\n65\t  scrutiny points CONFIRMED-OK: R3 grounding intact (skill/prompts/actions are real\n66\t  reads; `frobnicate`/`zzyzx` ungrounded claims still dropped); cache generate-once\n67\t  + force + no-poison-on-failure; R2 original byte-identical after continue + fresh\n68\t  worktree; endpoint token-gated; UI gate is a REAL Playwright clickâ†’panelâ†’summaryâ†’\n69\t  continue test (NOT grep-only); stdlib-only; never :8777. MINOR: produced-file\n70\t  labels not hyperlinked (doc links live in the summary block above â€” honest, not\n71\t  dangling); handler covered via Playwright rather than a dedicated HTTP unit test.\n72\t  Neither blocks. No FIX required.\n73\t- **UI VERIFY (orchestrator):** screenshot of a discovered planning session's panel\n74\t  â€” confirmed it shows the summary header + PLAN DOCUMENTS role links + \"Skill\n75\t  invoked: not recorded\" + \"Prompts asked: none recorded\" + \"Files produced:\n76\t  Master Plan / Impl Plan\" + the blue \"â–¶ Continue in a live session\" button\n77\t  (honest placeholders for the imported case; `ro-sec`=3).\n78\t- **COMMIT (scoped):** `6b781aa` â€” summarizer.py + anchor_gui.py +\n79\t  test_session_continue.py only (no runtime churn).\n80\t\n81\t## Wave 3 â€” Better project summaries (objective/purpose) + folded dashboard reflection â€” GREEN (2026-06-14)\n82\t\n83\t> Scope note: this wave ALSO delivers a user request raised mid-build â€” \"project-\n84\t> window changes should reflect on the main dashboard timely\" â€” folded in here\n85\t> because it touches the same dashboard-row/summary render path.\n86\t\n87\t- **EXECUTE** (fresh sub-agent): PART 1 â€” `summarizer.project_extraction_seed` adds\n88\t  per-lane activity; `_project_seed_prompt` rewritten to ask for a grounded 1-2\n89\t  sentence OBJECTIVE; `render_project_markdown` â†’ prose `## Objective`; project\n90\t  header renders the cached `Objective:` line; render path is cache-only (proven by\n91\t  stub-counter). PART 2 (folded) â€” read-only `GET /api/rnd/projects_html` (reuses\n92\t  `render_projects_view_html`), `#rndProjectsRows` container, `rndRowsRefresh()`\n93\t  poll(~15s)+visibilitychange+showView('rnd') in-place swap (diff-before-swap,\n94\t  hidden-view guard, failure-tolerant, no page reload).\n95\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 670 passed, 1 skipped (baseline 660+1, +10).\n96\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): SHIP â€” 0 BLOCKER, 1 MINOR (F1).** All\n97\t  7 points CONFIRMED-OK: cache-only render with a NON-VACUOUS counter proof (counter\n98\t  increments on a real run, stays put across renders); R3 grounding intact (per-lane\n99\t  activity is deterministic, ungrounded claims still dropped, honest \"No summary yet\",\n100\t  failed run no-poison); generate-once/force; the dashboard refresh swaps in place\n101\t  with real guards; UI gate is a REAL Playwright in-place-refresh test (NOT grep);\n102\t  stdlib-only + distro scan clean; never :8777. **F1 (MINOR):** the 15s poll\n103\t  re-rendered the default fragment, reverting a user's 30d rollup toggle + closing an\n104\t  open kebab.\n105\t- **FIX (orchestrator):** `rndRowsRefresh` now skips the swap while a kebab is open\n106\t  and preserves the active rollup window across the swap (capture before, re-apply\n107\t  after). New regression test `test_refresh_preserves_rollup_toggle_and_open_kebab`\n108\t  (scoped to `#rndProjectsRows` â€” the toggle markup also appears in a hidden view).\n109\t- **RE-GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 671 passed, 1 skipped. UI verified:\n110\t  rendered-DOM (`#rndProjectsRows` + JS present), real Playwright in-place refresh +\n111\t  toggle/kebab preservation, and an orchestrator screenshot of the project header\n112\t  showing the grounded objective line (\"â€¦energy-aware HVAC scheduler that pre-cools\n113\t  before peak prices\").\n114\t- **COMMIT (scoped):** `3bcac71` â€” summarizer.py + anchor_gui.py +\n115\t  test_project_summary_v5.py only (no runtime churn).\n116\t\n117\t## Wave 4 â€” Deliverable per Foreman build (resolve Â· backfill Â· list) â€” GREEN (2026-06-14)\n118\t\n119\t- **EXECUTE** (fresh sub-agent): `deliverables.resolve_build_deliverable` +\n120\t  `backfill_build_deliverables` (idempotent auto-pin) + read-only\n121\t  `GET /api/rnd/build_deliverable`; build panel renders its deliverable (`.bdeliv`)\n122\t  or the honest \"no deliverable pinned yet â€” pin one\"; Deliverables lane lists\n123\t  backfilled deliverables (auto-pin runs before the kanban render).\n124\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 683 passed, 1 skipped (baseline 671+1, +12).\n125\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): HALT â€” 2 BLOCKER, 1 MINOR.**\n126\t  **B1 (R4 fabrication):** the top signal used `summarizer.session_doc_roles`'s\n127\t  `deliverable` role, which is PROJECT-scoped (newest pin) â€” so EVERY build panel\n128\t  claimed the same artifact (e.g. anchor_gui.py) regardless of what it produced\n129\t  (proven with two probes). **B2 (false-green gate):** `test_resolve_from_doc_role`\n130\t  ENCODED the bug and there was ZERO multi-build-per-project coverage, so all 12\n131\t  tests + the real Playwright test passed on broken behavior. MINOR: `_is_plan_doc`\n132\t  startswith over-exclusion (readme*/handoff* â†’ false unresolved, never a\n133\t  fabric